# Drydock Window Decision

## Current Model

Elena Vasquez approved the **SG-REFIT drydock** window opening on **drydock window 2026-05-18**, formally starting the **seaglass drydock** cycle at berth 4 heavy-lift zone. MV Seaglass is Seaglass-only through refit sea trial. Victor Hale confirmed the spare thrust bearing crate is port-side; hull penetration waits on his sign-off but prep work may begin. Fuel-system purge sequencing was deferred to the next morning sync.

## Evidence

- `2026-05-18-drydock-window-opens` - Elena Vasquez email states **SG-REFIT drydock** is officially open; **drydock window 2026-05-18** starts now with berth 4 heavy-lift zone reserved for **seaglass drydock** through refit sea trial; Victor Hale confirms thrust bearing staged before hull penetration is cleared.

## Use In Work

- Treat 2026-05-18 as the authoritative drydock start for SG-REFIT berth holds, crane windows, and sailing impact grids.
- Block hull penetration work until Victor Hale signs off on thrust bearing staging per his drydock opening note.

## Limits

This decision opens the drydock window only — it does not settle fuel-line purge sequence adoption, crane booking date (confirmed 2026-05-19 separately), or sea trial scheduling on 2026-06-05.

## Connections

- [[elena-vasquez]] - Fleet Maintenance Director who approved and opened the drydock window.
- [[sg-refit]] - Refit project whose drydock cycle this decision starts.
- [[mv-seaglass]] - Vessel occupying berth 4 through the approved drydock window.
- [[drydock-berth-4]] - Heavy-lift berth where the SG-REFIT drydock window applies.
=== END FILE ===

