# Change Order Cap Decision

## Current Model

Glenn Wexler set the **change order cap** for **P9-GATE** at **$18400** without VP sign-off during the 2026-05-04 procurement week open. Anything above routes to Glenn's desk plus Elena Vasquez if fleet-adjacent. The cap covers scope on the P9-GATE WBS including night lighting Victor Dunn tied to gate side only — Glenn warned against burying gangway contingency in gate change orders. At Q2 closeout preview Glenn reaffirmed the **p9-gate** ceiling held after the Turnstile delivery slip.

## Evidence

- `2026-05-04-procurement-week-open` - Glenn Wexler sets **change order cap** for **p9-gate** at **$18400** without VP sign-off; anything above routes to his desk plus Elena Vasquez if fleet-adjacent; Glenn confirms cap covers night lighting on P9-GATE WBS and warns against burying gangway contingency in gate change orders.
- `2026-06-08-q2-closeout-preview` - Glenn reaffirms original **change order cap** on **p9-gate** remains **$18400** without VP sign-off and reports the project stayed inside that ceiling after the Turnstile gate delivery slip to May 28.

## Use In Work

- Route P9-GATE change orders through Glenn Wexler and hold them under **$18400** unless VP sign-off is obtained.
- Keep gangway contingency requests on P9-GANG cost codes — do not fold them into gate change orders under this cap.

## Limits

This cap applies to P9-GATE WBS only — P9-GANG has a separate cost code track. Victor Dunn's rejected **$62000 contingency** gangway envelope is governed by a different decision.

## Connections

- [[glenn-wexler]] - Procurement Finance Controller who set and reaffirmed the cap.
- [[p9-gate-retrofit]] - Gate project whose change orders this ceiling governs.
- [[decision-reject-gangway-contingency]] - Related rejection of duplicate gangway contingency outside this cap.
- [[rule-change-order-routing]] - Standing rule for how change orders route through Glenn's desk.
=== END FILE ===

