# Critical Path P9-Gate Decision

## Current Model

Juno Castillo declared **P9-GATE** the **critical path** for Q2 Pier 9 closeout on **2026-05-13**, logging the date in the Q2 Terminal Readiness Playbook. Gangway can flex; gate cannot. Marcus Holt reordered the closure grid giving gate crew priority at berth 9B west while Bridgeway stays on the east apron. The call stands after Turnstile Dynamics slipped gate delivery to **2026-05-28** — only the date changed, not the critical-path designation.

## Evidence

- `2026-05-13-critical-path-declaration` - Juno Castillo calls **p9-gate** the **critical path** for Q2 pier 9 closeout with **2026-05-13** logged in the playbook; Marcus Holt reorders closure grid giving gate crew priority at berth 9B west; Juno reminds crews no stacking gate and gangway shifts on the same berth.

## Use In Work

- Prioritize P9-GATE berth windows, badge access, and commissioning over P9-GANG flex windows when schedules conflict.
- When Elena Vasquez or others ask which Pier 9 stream drives closeout, cite gate not gangway per the 2026-05-13 call.

## Limits

Critical-path status does not override Marcus Holt's back-to-back shift ban on the same Pier 9 berth or Priya's load-test certificate gate on gangway passenger use.

## Connections

